dynrec: add SPARC V9 64-bit backend

Derived from the PowerPC backends. Generated code runs in its own
register window, values passed to C functions are zero-extended as
required by the ABI. Blocks return directly with ret/restore, and on
CPUs with a coherent I-cache (UltraSPARC III and later) a single flush
per block is issued.

The code cache is mapped right below the executable (DRC_CACHE_ALLOC),
so helpers are reached with a direct call; only calls that may be
replaced by flags optimization keep a padded stanza. Memory accesses
look up the TLB inline and use direct host pointers little-endian via
ASI_PRIMARY_LITTLE (DRC_USE_INLINE_MEMORY). Branch conditions are
evaluated inline from the lazy flags, guessing the last flags operation
of the block and checking lflags.type at runtime (DRC_USE_INLINE_FLAGS).
Base registers address core_dynrec, cache, cache_blocks and the TLB.

Performance on a Sun UltraSPARC IIIi (sun4u, 1 CPU), DOSBox cycles=max,
machine=svga_s3, SB Pro, measured under Xvfb:

  Test                    normal core   dynamic core   speedup
  3DBENCH                 18.1 fps      40.0 fps       2.21x
  Doom -timedemo demo3     7.5 fps      18.7 fps       2.49x
                          (10012 rt)    (3985 rt, 2134 gametics)
  Quake +timedemo demo1    2.3 fps       9.7 fps       4.22x
                          (418.0 s)     (90.1 s, 969 frames)

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

